WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.687
Apple Silicon systems can run local chat interfaces, web UIs, local inference APIs,

00:00:04.687 --> 00:00:07.156
coding tools, document workflows, and private assistants.

00:00:07.156 --> 00:00:10.332
Once a local model is served through an endpoint,

00:00:10.332 --> 00:00:13.507
it can become part of a broader application workflow.

00:00:13.507 --> 00:00:17.035
That is useful, but it also changes the risk profile.

00:00:17.035 --> 00:00:20.211
The model is no longer only an interactive experiment.

00:00:20.211 --> 00:00:23.033
It is a service other tools may call.

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:27.267
Localhost binding is a safer default for private inference services because it

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:29.384
limits access to the local machine.

00:00:29.384 --> 00:00:33.265
LAN access can be useful for a homelab or team environment,

00:00:33.265 --> 00:00:35.029
but it should be deliberate.

00:00:35.029 --> 00:00:36.441
Reverse proxies, authentication, TLS,

00:00:36.441 --> 00:00:42.086
and access policy may be needed at a high level if other users or devices connect.

00:00:42.086 --> 00:00:45.967
Avoid accidental exposure of a local model endpoint to untrusted networks.

00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:49.142
Applications that call local models should be scoped carefully.

00:00:49.142 --> 00:00:54.082
A coding tool, document assistant, or private chat interface may send sensitive prompts, files,

00:00:54.082 --> 00:00:56.198
or context to the inference endpoint.

00:00:56.198 --> 00:00:58.668
If several applications share one local service,

00:00:58.668 --> 00:01:02.902
operators should understand which data flows through it, whether logs are retained,

00:01:02.902 --> 00:01:05.372
and whether different workflows should be separated.

00:01:05.372 --> 00:01:08.547
Serving local models is not just a convenience feature.

00:01:08.547 --> 00:01:12.428
It requires decisions about access control, logging, retention, uptime, update timing,

00:01:12.428 --> 00:01:13.487
and failure behavior.

00:01:13.487 --> 00:01:16.309
Treat prompts and outputs as potentially sensitive data.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.073
Local inference can improve privacy,

00:01:18.073 --> 00:01:22.660
but only when service exposure and surrounding application behavior are managed with intention.
